- **Exclusion note:** this report is written as `.md.excluded` because **no independent or first‑party evidence for a model literally named "Gemini 4 Argo" could be found on any authoritative source**, and its curated specs contradict Google's real, closely‑named flagship. Every search across `blog.google`, the DeepMind model card, Google Cloud, CNBC, OpenRouter and llm‑stats returns **Gemini 4 *Argon*** (announced 2026‑09‑30, GA on Google Cloud 2026‑10‑13) — a *separate* registry line already present as `model/gemini-4-argon/`. There is **no model card, blog post, API page, or benchmark row for `gemini-4-argo`**. The curated `meta.json` ("200K ctx, $3.50/$17.50, Text/code/image in") matches **nothing** published: real Gemini 4 Argon lists **up to 1M output at $2/$10**. So `gemini-4-argo` reads as a **phantom / mis‑spelled duplicate** of Argon. Per `RULES.md`, a findings file is self‑excluded (never fabricated) when there are zero verified benchmarks for the exact ID; attributing Gemini‑4‑**Argon**'s verified numbers (DeepSWE v1.1 77.9, $2/$10, 1M output) to the `gemini-4-argo` slug would reattribute a *different* model whose specs also disagree, so no scores are asserted. Any capability review belongs in the `gemini-4-argon/` entry.

